Product Catalog API

This is a simple backend project for a take-home test. It lets you upload a CSV of products, save them in a database, and then search and manage them using an API.

How to Run this thing

Its pretty easy to get this running on your computer.

What you need first:

Node.js (like version 16 or newer is good)

npm (this comes with Node.js)

Installation

First, open your terminal and go to this project folder.

Then just run this command to install all the packages the project needs.

npm install


Starting the Server

To start the server, you just run this command.

npm start


You will see a message like Server running on http://localhost:3000. That means its working.

API Docs

All the API routes start with /api/v1.

1. Upload CSV File

Endpoint: POST /api/v1/upload

Description: You send a CSV file here to add products to database. It check every row for errors.

How to send: Use form-data, with the key as file and value is your CSV file.

Example Request (using Postman or curl):

POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/upload
Body (form-data):
Key: file
Value: (select your products.csv file)


Success Response:

{
    "message": "CSV processing complete. 20 rows were analyzed.",
    "stored_count": 20,
    "failed_count": 0,
    "failures": []
}


2. Get All Products

Endpoint: GET /api/v1/products

Description: This gets you a list of all products in the database. It has pagination.

Query Params:

page (optional): which page number you want. Default is 1.

limit (optional): how many products on one page. Default is 10.

Example Request:
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/products?page=1&limit=5

Response:

{
    "total_products": 20,
    "current_page": 1,
    "page_limit": 5,
    "products": [
        {
            "sku": "TSHIRT-RED-001",
            "name": "Classic Cotton T-Shirt",
            // ... other fields
        }
    ]
}


3. Search for Products

Endpoint: GET /api/v1/products/search

Description: Find products based on filters.

Query Params:

brand (optional): Search by brand or product name.

color (optional): Filter by color.

minPrice (optional): Minimum price.

maxPrice (optional): Maximum price.

Example Request:
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/products/search?brand=Urban&maxPrice=1000

Response:

{
    "total_found": 2,
    "current_page": 1,
    "page_limit": 10,
    "products": [
        {
            "sku": "TSHIRT-GRY-S",
            "name": "Graphic Tee",
            "brand": "Urban Edge",
            // ... other fields
        }
    ]
}


4. Update a Product

Endpoint: PATCH /api/v1/products/:sku

Description: Change details for one product using its SKU.

Example Request:
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/v1/products/TSHIRT-RED-001

Body (raw JSON):

{
    "price": 599,
    "quantity": 25
}


5. Delete a Product

Endpoint: DELETE /api/v1/products/:sku

Description: Delete one product by its SKU.

Example Request:
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/v1/products/TSHIRT-RED-001

